        "instruction": {
          "title": "Comparing Mars, Jupiter, and Saturn",
          "description": "The heliocentric view now includes Jupiter (5.2 AU) and Saturn (9.5 AU). Step through a retrograde event for each planet. Mars loops about 15 degrees, Jupiter about 10 degrees, Saturn about 7 degrees. More distant planets show smaller loops because Earth's orbital motion subtends a smaller angle from farther away \u2014 similar to how nearby objects shift more than distant ones as you move your head."
        },
